  "description": "The meme is designed for audiences who are part of or sympathetic to anti-LGBTQ+ religious or cultural communities. It targets individuals who may use or propagate misinformation about biblical texts to justify prejudice against LGBTQ+ people, particularly by misrepresenting Leviticus 20:13 as a command from Jesus. The meme's intent is to reinforce religious condemnation themes and promote harmful stereotypes, appealing to those who interpret scripture in a literalist or exclusionary manner.",
